.TH NEXUS 1 "November 2026" "nexus-cli 0.1.0" "NexusOS Engineering Edition"
.SH NAME
nexus \- NexusOS Engineering Edition command-line toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nexus
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nexus
reports system, development, infrastructure and local-AI status on NexusOS
and other Ubuntu-based systems. Commands are read-only unless stated
otherwise; privileged steps are shown first and run through
.BR sudo (8)
only after interactive confirmation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
CLI, operating system and Python versions.
.TP
.B help \fR[\fIGROUP\fR]
Help for all commands or one group.
.TP
.B system info\fR | \fBhealth\fR | \fBupdate\fR | \fBcleanup
System information; read-only health checks (exit 1 on failure); APT upgrade
preview with confirmation (\fB\-\-refresh\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR); cleanup preview
(\fB\-\-apply\fR to clean after per-item confirmation).
.TP
.B dev list\fR | \fBdev create fastapi \fINAME\fR | \fBdev create react \fINAME
Templates and toolchains; generate a FastAPI project offline; scaffold React
with Vite via npm (\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
.B cloud status
Detect cloud and Kubernetes CLIs. Credentials are never read or printed.
.TP
.B infra status\fR | \fBinfra containers
Docker, KVM, libvirt and Podman status; list Docker containers via the Engine API.
.TP
.B ai status\fR | \fBai models
Detect Ollama and list locally installed models. Models are never downloaded.
.PP
Most read-only commands accept \fB\-\-json\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 failure or failed health check; 2 invalid input;
3 missing dependency or unreachable service; 4 cancelled; 70 internal error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama endpoint (default http://127.0.0.1:11434). URLs with credentials are rejected.
.TP
.B DOCKER_HOST
Only unix:// sockets are queried.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/os-release\fR, \fI/usr/lib/nexusos/release
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR docker (1),
.BR ollama (1)
.SH AUTHOR
NexusOS was crafted by Sanjay, with the NexusOS contributors.
